{% extends 'layouts/shell.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Settings — Gomrok Admin{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1 class="page-title" style="font-size:22px;margin-bottom:6px">Settings</h1>

<div style="border:1px dashed var(--border);border-radius:9px;padding:22px 20px;max-width:640px">
  <div style="font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px">No settings screen yet</div>
  <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.5">
    This nav entry exists to match the admin panel's design shell, but there is no
    admin-editable settings domain or database table behind it. Gomrok's configuration today
    is plain environment variables loaded once at boot — not rows an operator can view or
    change from this panel.
  </p>
  <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
    If a real operational-settings feature is wanted (for example a maintenance-mode toggle or
    a feature flag an admin can flip live), that needs its own database design, proposed and
    confirmed first — not invented to fill this placeholder.
  </p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
